  <data name="zDropEditColumnStyleInfo1.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This field is used to reference a type of imported food foreign certification document from an overseas government. Where Quarantine Document Type is supplied, Quarantine Document Number must also be provided and the Quarantine Document Type code supplied must exist in the EDI reference data. Up to 10 pairs of Document Type and Document Number may be provided on each tariff line.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="zTextBoxColumnStyleInfo1.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This field, along with Quarantine Document Type, allows the broker to nominate overseas government issued certification for food consignments. It is used to identify the particular document number. This field must be supplied when the Quarantine Document Type is supplied. Up to 10 pairs of Document Type and Document Number may be provided on each tariff line.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="zCodeFindBoxColumnStyleInfo1.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Quarantine Premises ID, previously known to Quarantine users as the AEP Location Code is an importer/broker-nominated field. The importer / broker must be accredited with Quarantine as a part of the Containerised Cargo Clearance (CCC) Scheme for FCL, FCX, LCL and Automatic Entry Processing (AEP) Scheme. It is a unique ID for premises that are authorised to receive cargo that is required to undergo Quarantine treatments/ procedures. The premises ID is nominated by the broker according to their preference of authorised Quarantine premises. These premises have been approved by the Director of Quarantine for the performance of quarantine under section 46A of the Quarantine Act 1908. As part of the changeover to CMR, 5 character Quarantine Premises ID will be used instead of the currently familiar 3 character AEP Location Codes. This field is generally supplied together with the Quarantine Processing Type.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="zDropEditColumnStyleInfo2.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Quarantine Processing Type, previously known as the AEP Activity Code, is an importer/broker-nominated code indicating an action Quarantine should take with a consignment.The importer/broker must be accredited with Quarantine as a part of the CCC/AEP Scheme. The Accredited Person selects the Quarantine Processing Type from the Quarantine Processing Type field. The Quarantine Processing Type indicates to Quarantine what documents the Accredited Person has accepted and what activity should be performed</value>
  </data>
